Shard repair worker exits after first idle timeout
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/c15427b9f88c8191a80f69b4bd4687a3?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: informational (attack path: ignore)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit [`b5a83478`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/b5a83478) (`Keep shard repair worker alive after idle waits`).

The shard repair worker now distinguishes shutdown from an ordinary empty-queue polling timeout. If `wait_for_placed_segment_shard_repair_work` returns `None` while the stop flag is not set, the worker remains alive and continues its loop instead of exiting. It only breaks out of the loop when the coordinator is actually stopping.

The regression test now synchronizes on the worker reaching the idle-timeout branch before enqueueing repair work, so it directly covers the original failure mode without relying on a fixed sleep. The test hook is scoped to the coordinator's storage-cluster registry key, preventing another in-process shard repair worker from satisfying the hook under parallel test execution.

Verification for the fix:
- `cargo nextest run -p server-core shard_repair_worker_repairs_read_discovered_corrupt_shard`
- `cargo nextest run -p server-core`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- `cargo nextest run`

